# Agent, editor and shell config a sandboxed coder run may leave in the work tree (not
# project files). Under a harness's OS sandbox, Claude Code writes an empty placeholder for
# each of these to protect the path; they must stay out of the way so `tools/guards.sh`'s
# clean-tree check passes — it lists untracked files by .gitignore alone, so the runner's
# .git/info/exclude does not reach it (see adapters.CLAUDE_PLACEHOLDERS; kept in sync by a
# test). `.idea/` is covered at the top; `.claude/settings.json` stays tracked.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.profile
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.ripgreprc
/.mcp.json
/.idea
/.vscode
/.claude/agents
/.claude/commands
/.claude/hooks
/.claude/launch.json
/.claude/loop.md
/.claude/output-styles
/.claude/routines
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/skills
/.claude/workflows
